            "review_text": "ahl23\nPennsylvania11 contributions\n0\nOMG soooo goood!!!!\nMar 2019 • Business\nOur taxi driver recommended this local restaurant and we are so glad he did! It was soo good and inexpensive that we returned the next night! Nem Nuong is grilled pork. Our order came with grilled pork, crunchy shells, fresh vegetables that you roll in rice paper and dip in a sauce. Keep in mind that this is a place for locals, so eat at your own risk of getting traveler's diarrhea. That being said, we ate here two days in a row and did not get sick. We did not eat all the vegetables given to us just to be sure. We had two orders of this dish plus a soda and I think our bill was just under $8 USD. Taxi ride from our hotel (Ariyanna Condotel) was about $1.50. I cannot wait to come back to Nha Trang and eat here again. The staff were very nice too! I believe the owner was chilling a few seats near us and he was very friendly and helpful in calling a cab for us when we finished our meal.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 4, 2019",
